        <p>Polish consumers skew toward <strong>high-strength pouches</strong> (12–20mg) and <strong>mint flavours</strong>, but—uniquely—they're adventurous with fruit profiles. Blueberry, watermelon, and berry blends outsell fruit options in Nordic markets. Coffee and tobacco flavours remain niche; dessert and candy flavours are growing but still secondary to mint and fruit.</p>

